Resource format and graphics behavior are informed by ScummVM's Tinsel engine:
https://github.com/scummvm/scummvm/tree/96b42d42bc8533953bdd701db059cc33c839a9ff/engines/tinsel

ScummVM is copyright its contributors. Upstream attribution:
https://github.com/scummvm/scummvm/blob/96b42d42bc8533953bdd701db059cc33c839a9ff/COPYRIGHT

In particular, graphics.rs implements the DOS tile behavior documented by
graphics.cpp (WrtNonZero and DrawObject), handle.cpp (GetImage and GetPalette),
and scene.h (resource handle layout). resource.rs uses the index and chunk
formats documented in handle.cpp and scn.cpp. This is not a clean-room project.

script.rs follows pcode.cpp instruction and frame semantics. library.rs preserves
the DW1_CODES ordering from tinlib.cpp. scene.rs uses scene.cpp and handle.cpp
scene, entrance, and actor formats at the same pinned revision.

film.rs uses film.h and multiobj.h layouts. startup.rs follows declaration
semantics in tinlib.cpp, cursor.cpp, dialogs.cpp, actors.cpp, and mareels.cpp.

animation.rs follows anim.cpp. compositor.rs uses object.cpp and multiobj.cpp
animation-point semantics. engine.rs follows the initial scene and library
behavior in scene.cpp, bg.cpp, and tinlib.cpp; scheduling remains provisional.

audio.rs follows the original DOS PCM archive and channel behavior in sound.cpp.
PLAYSAMPLE, STOPSAMPLE, and WAITFRAME integration uses tinlib.cpp and play.cpp.

The game data, artwork, dialogue, and audio remain separate proprietary assets.
No playable game resources are included in the source distribution.
The documentary runtime screenshots and animated montage in docs/media depict
original game artwork. That artwork remains the property of its respective
rights holders and is not covered by the runtime source license.
The polygon reader and cooperative queue are informed by ScummVM's
engines/tinsel/polygons.cpp and common/coroutines.cpp at the pinned revision.

Actor startup state and WAITKEY behavior are informed by pinned ScummVM
engines/tinsel/actors.cpp and engines/tinsel/tinlib.cpp.

Music archive and XMIDI decoding are informed by pinned ScummVM
engines/tinsel/music.cpp and audio/midiparser_xmidi.cpp.

The sequencer also uses behavior from audio/midiparser.cpp.
Control and cursor state use the V1 behavior from tinlib.cpp, events.cpp,
and cursor.cpp at the pinned ScummVM revision.
String decoding, fonts, and PRINT behavior are informed by strres.cpp,
handle.cpp, text.cpp, and tinlib.cpp at that revision.
vendor/rustysynth contains RustySynth 1.3.7, copyright Nobuaki Tanaka,
under its retained MIT license. Local modifications are documented there.
vendor/samples contains its two upstream SoundFont parser test fixtures.
The locally downloaded TimGM6mb development SoundFont is not included in
this repository; its separate GPL-2 notice is retained with the local asset.

random.rs translates the generator in common/random.cpp and RandomFn in
engines/tinsel/tinlib.cpp at the pinned ScummVM revision (GPL-3.0-or-later).

Deferred scene transitions and fade tables follow engines/tinsel/tinsel.cpp,
tinlib.cpp, bg.cpp, and faders.cpp at the same pinned revision.

Scripted scroll motion and completion behavior follow engines/tinsel/scroll.cpp
and tinlib.cpp at the pinned revision.

Normal/talk film arbitration follows engines/tinsel/play.cpp t1PlayReel and
actors.cpp at the pinned revision.

Initial mover placement and scale selection follow engines/tinsel/movers.cpp,
polygons.cpp, scene.h, and movers.h at the pinned revision.

Direct walking steps and facing calculations follow engines/tinsel/move.cpp
NewCoOrdinates and GetDirection at the pinned revision.
